# The Keyboard settings page: every command with the keys that run it, and a recorder that takes a
# new shortcut by having it pressed.
#
# `settings key press <chord>` is the recorder being offered a chord — the step after a key event
# has been turned into one — so this covers what the page decides: what is refused, what is
# somebody else's, and that an assignment reaches the keymap, the menus and the palette at once.

tree .
refresh

settings keyboard
shot 01-keyboard
assert-key-row New tab Ctrl+T
assert-key-row Back Backspace,Alt+Left
assert-key-row Duplicate tab Ctrl+Shift+K
assert-key-row Close other tabs none

# --- Filtering: by name, by category, by shortcut ---

settings key filter flat
assert-key-row Toggle flat view Ctrl+B
assert-key-row New tab absent
settings key filter ctrl+shift
assert-key-row Search this PC Ctrl+Shift+F
assert-key-row New tab absent
shot 02-filtered-by-shortcut
settings key filter

# --- Changing one ---

settings key select view.flat
settings key change
assert-key-recorder Press the new shortcut for
shot 03-recording

# A key that types is refused, and the recorder goes on listening.
settings key press B
assert-key-recorder can’t be used
settings key press Ctrl+K
assert-key-row Toggle flat view Ctrl+K
assert-gesture view.flat Ctrl+K

# --- A chord that is somebody else's is offered, never taken silently ---

settings key select tab.close-others
settings key change
settings key press Ctrl+T
assert-key-recorder already runs
# The recorder has stopped listening, so the keyboard can reach the Reassign button.
assert-key-recorder Reassign it to
shot 04-conflict
# Nothing has moved yet.
assert-key-row New tab Ctrl+T
settings key reassign
assert-key-row Close other tabs Ctrl+T
assert-key-row New tab none
shot 05-reassigned

# --- A second shortcut, taking one away, and putting it back ---

settings key select tab.new
settings key add
settings key press Ctrl+N
assert-key-row New tab Ctrl+N
settings key add
settings key press Ctrl+Shift+Y
assert-key-row New tab Ctrl+N,Ctrl+Shift+Y

settings key select nav.refresh
settings key remove
assert-key-row Refresh none
settings key reset
assert-key-row Refresh F5

# --- Find by key ---

settings key find
settings key press Ctrl+K
assert-key-row Toggle flat view Ctrl+K
assert-key-row Refresh absent
settings key filter

# --- The settings survive the page, and Reset all undoes them ---

settings close
# Checked out here rather than on the page: while Settings is up, every shortcut about the
# folders is silenced, the rebound ones included.
assert-key Ctrl+K list view.flat
assert-key Ctrl+B list none
assert-key Ctrl+T list tab.close-others
assert-key Ctrl+N list tab.new
select notes.txt
menu files 06-menu-after-rebinding
palette
palette type toggle flat
assert-palette-selected Toggle flat view
shot 07-palette-shows-new-shortcut
palette close

settings keyboard
settings key reset-all
assert-key-row New tab Ctrl+T
assert-key-row Toggle flat view Ctrl+B
assert-key-row Close other tabs none
settings close
assert-key Ctrl+T list tab.new
assert-key Ctrl+B list view.flat

# --- From the palette: "change shortcut" lands here, already listening ---

palette
palette type new tab
palette shortcut
assert-palette-closed
assert-key-recorder Press the new shortcut for “New tab”
shot 08-from-the-palette
settings key press Ctrl+Shift+Y
assert-key-row New tab Ctrl+Shift+Y
settings key reset-all
settings close

assert-not-launched
